## 1. Scope

This reference covers prefabricated cold shrink terminations and straight joints applied to 0.6/1 kV distribution cable, and the parameters a purchaser normally fixes before a size is quoted. It is written for the person who has to match an accessory to a cable that is already on site, not the person choosing the cable.

## 2. Construction

- Factory-expanded EPDM or silicone sleeve held under compression on a removable spiral supporting core.
- The core is unwound on site, so the sleeve recovers by its own stored elastic energy and no flame or heat source is needed.
- Sealing is completed by mastic strips plus an outer sleeve or adhesive layer closing the cable-to-accessory interface.
- Because recovery is elastic rather than thermal, the recovered wall stays in permanent radial compression on the cable insulation.

## 3. Typical specification range

| Parameter | Typical value | Notes |
